## Content and authoring

The original 20,659-byte Markdown and 45,209-byte authored source retain the atomic snapshot/SourceAdmission preamble before the first Section. Preserve this preamble and its ownership/index/accounting qualification rather than treating it as disposable progress text. Paragraph phrasing is intentionally edited for readability, with shorter sentences and explanatory shared-storage Anno; the technical obligations remain equivalent by full-text comparison.

Especially checked: same-storage versus independently decoded snapshot proofs and atomic/non-atomic behavior; clone versus conservative Compare cost; no pointer-derived wire identity; edit/admission atomic commit versus retained consumed resources; source scalar/CRLF/BOM positions; schema and display-kind separation; lossless versus canonical print; ForeignClosure owner/guest tables, original Origin IDs/digest and R046 namespace distinction; all inverse map paths and empty-span insertion anchor; generated diagnostic/rename restrictions; FactAuthority scope/import/endpoint permissions and reserved-ID FactDelta rules; report/fix conflicts and source closure; first event-overflow stopping and sticky earlier StopReason; retained resource usage and source admission; partial values not checked proofs.

