Normal prose uses sentence literals; explicit sentences contain real code and retain appropriate Ruby/Concat. The shared immutable storage explanation is an Anno whose base includes the English storage word and kanji Ruby, rather than misusing Ruby for a whole semantic gloss. Kana, Latin words and punctuation stay outside Japanese Ruby bases. Empty-interval/empty-span くう readings are not independently classified as errors merely because the preferred reading of 空文字 in chapter06 was からもじ.

## Structures, code and dependency closure

Ten unique Sections: policy, source_range, schema_kind, token_syntax, views, origins, names_relations, facts_authority, diagnostics_events, budgets_results. Forty-one Paragraphs, no Lists, Tables, code blocks, explicit breaks, parallel, Foreign or Math constructors. The single nested facts_authority Section remains last in names_relations Body and preserves the original h3; remaining sections are h2. The article preamble precedes all Sections, so the annotated Body ordering constraint is satisfied.

All eighteen original inline-code payloads remain present and ordered; draft has nineteen spans because the originally plain second [start,end) in FactDelta is now code. Preserve the exact half-open interval text. This markup change does not modify interval semantics, but actual code output remains a final rendering check.

Neither original nor draft has an actual link. Thus there is no Relative/passive artifact dependency; named files/types/operations are retained as original prose or code. Current registry has thirteen pages and does not yet register chapter02; the absence of chapter02 itself is expected before cutover. No renderer capability extension is indicated by this source inspection.

